1x8j|n|A precious stone of a carmine red color, sometimes verging to violet, or intermediate between carmine and hyacinth red. It is a red crystallized variety of corundum. ; The color of a ruby; carmine red; a red tint. ; That which has the color of the ruby, as red wine. Hence, a red blain or carbuncle. ; See Agate, n., 2. ; Any species of South American humming birds of the genus Clytolaema. The males have a ruby-colored throat or breast.	N:1hnk,88,2;1hnj,41,1~1hnk,88,2;1hnj,41,1
