1xd7|n|of Ring ; imp. & p. p. of Ring. ; A floor timber in a ship. ; One of the rounds of a ladder. ; One of the stakes of a cart; a spar; a heavy staff. ; One of the radial handles projecting from the rim of a steering wheel; also, one of the pins or trundles of a lantern wheel.	a:9je,81,3;1atl,70,2~9je,81,3;1atl,70,2	n:1ioh,24,2~1ioh,24,2
