1xdf|a|Moving or advancing by running. ; Having a running gait; not a trotter or pacer. ; trained and kept for running races; as, a running horse. ; Successive; one following the other without break or intervention; -- said of periods of time; as, to be away two days running; to sow land two years running. ; Flowing; easy; cursive; as, a running hand. ; Continuous; keeping along step by step; as, he stated the facts with a running explanation. ; Extending by a slender climbing or trailing stem; as, a running vine. ; Discharging pus; as, a running sore.	j:1hnw,69,4;1pj,61,8;1a22,60,34;w86,59,7;1khi,57,6;1vv3,56,4;1kh5,53,7;1al3,50,69;1782,50,16;w60,49,26;12ln,48,53;185n,48,41;1ehr,46,22;1r1l,43,56;iy9,43,13~3b2,12,193;24m6,34,128;4jf,15,118;2go7,32,80;1al3,50,69;iya,39,56;1r1l,43,56;200i,28,53;12ln,48,53;12o,13,53;185n,48,41;1a22,60,34;1a4m,25,34;tjs,22,34;eiv,28,26	e:gmm,35,4;gfm,26,12;ism,21,80;1qlp,17,1;2009,6,10;p6j,6,6;21yr,5,2;2l1,4,67;zk,1,3~ism,21,80;2l1,4,67;gfm,26,12;2009,6,10;p6j,6,6;gmm,35,4;zk,1,3;21yr,5,2;1qlp,17,1
